{# Arista EOS — Base Configuration Template
   ==========================================
   WHY ARISTA SYNTAX IS DIFFERENT (for interview):
   Arista EOS is Linux-based and has a cleaner CLI syntax than Cisco IOS.
   For example, Arista uses "management api http-commands" for eAPI
   (REST API access to the switch), which Cisco doesn't have natively.
   This is why Arista dominates data centers — API-first design.
#}
!
! {{ inventory_hostname }} — Generated by TradeNet Fabric Automation
! Site: {{ site_name }} | Role: {{ role }}
!
hostname {{ inventory_hostname }}
!
! === Users ===
username admin privilege 15 role network-admin secret {{ vault_device_password }}
!
! === Management Interface ===
interface Loopback0
   description MGMT-LOOPBACK
   ip address {{ loopback_ip }}
   no shutdown
!
! === DNS ===
{% for dns in dns_servers %}
ip name-server {{ dns }}
{% endfor %}
dns domain tradenet.local
!
! === NTP ===
{% for ntp in ntp_servers %}
ntp server {{ ntp }}
{% endfor %}
!
! === Syslog ===
logging host {{ syslog.server }}
logging facility {{ syslog.facility }}
logging level {{ syslog.severity }}
logging source-interface Loopback0
!
! === SNMP ===
snmp-server community {{ snmp.community }} ro
snmp-server location {{ snmp.location }}
snmp-server contact {{ snmp.contact }}
!
! === Banner ===
banner motd
{{ banner }}
EOF
!
! === SSH ===
management ssh
   idle-timeout 60
   no shutdown
!
! === eAPI (Arista's REST API) ===
{# WHY eAPI (for interview):
   Arista's eAPI gives us REST API access to the switch — we can
   query state, push config, and collect telemetry via HTTP/JSON.
   This is how our SDN controller communicates with Arista switches
   (in addition to NETCONF). Cisco requires a separate agent for
   similar functionality. This is Arista's biggest advantage. #}
management api http-commands
   protocol https
   no shutdown
!
! === Management ACL ===
ip access-list {{ management_acl.name }}
{% for network in management_acl.networks %}
   permit ip {{ network }} any
{% endfor %}
   deny ip any any log
!
! === Services ===
no ip routing  {# Re-enabled when OSPF/BGP is configured #}
service routing protocols model multi-agent
{# multi-agent routing: Each routing protocol runs as a separate Linux
   process. This means a BGP crash doesn't take down OSPF. Arista
   exclusive feature — important for reliability. #}
!
end
